            <ArticleTitle>[A continuous murmur in female patient after traffic injury].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1283-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of a 33 year-old female with continuous murmur was admitted to the hospital for diagnostic purposes. TEE was inconclusive. Coronary angiography revealed an aneurysm of left anterior descending with the fistula to the right ventricle. The patient underwent implantation of inset of left internal mammary artery graft and ligation of fistula during open heart surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
